+# Tool input validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+The registry validates model-supplied input against each tool's declared JSON Schema before execution.
+
+- Invalid required fields, types, and enum values produce a descriptive tool result without invoking the executor; valid input, including extra properties, reaches it unchanged, and unknown tool names still throw ([validated by: rejects invalid input before execution while preserving valid input](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L11)).
+- A static schema that cannot compile fails at registration with the tool name ([validated by: rejects a malformed static schema at registration with the tool name](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L38)).
+- A function-valued definition uses the schema resolved for each call, and rejection text and logs exclude input values ([validated by: validates each dynamically resolved schema without exposing input values](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L45)).
